#VAR(Table, TABLE)
#ADDTBL("../encoding.tbl", Table)
#ACTIVETBL(Table)
#VAR(PTR, CUSTOMPOINTER)
#CREATEPTR(PTR, "LINEAR", 0, 16)
#JMP($00000C0A)

#WRITE(PTR, $000004B2)
Two hours prior.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000518)
The light of the sunset bathed a hospital room in a vibrant orange.%NAll was silent, as if time itself had stopped.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000528)
Only a single person was present.%NCompletely still, as if asleep, sat a boy in a wheelchair.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000538)
It was around the time of day when one would find nurses rushing%Naround the hospital, serving patients their dinners. And yet, no%Nsuch signs of activity made their way to the room.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000570)
A moment later, the silence was broken by the sound of a door%Nopening.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005BA)
A lone girl entered the room.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005CA)
The boy in the wheelchair lifted his head to acknowledge her, but%Ndid not speak.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005DA)
For a moment, the girl hesitated at the entrance.
<LINE>
Looking around the room, she could sense a faint aura of%Nloneliness emanating from it.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000005F2)
The drab-looking room was minimal in size and reeked of%Ndisinfectant.
<LINE>
This was where the two of them spent their days.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000602)
An isolated location, eternally unknown to the rest of humanity.
<LINE>
Not a single soul—be they a doctor, nurse, friend, or %Nrelative—ever came to visit.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000612)
The boy and girl rarely exchanged words with one another.
<LINE>
The boy had been hospitalized, and for a whole year had been%Ncomatose. Only just a month ago had he awoken.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000622)
The girl had been essentially using his room as a place to stay.
<LINE>
However, as much as she did trust him, their relationship had%Nnothing to do with any sort of romantic or sexual attraction.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000632)
Her only goal was to repay her debt to the boy.%NNothing more, nothing less.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000642)
The boy was intentionally cold and distant, having even told her%Nnot to return once before—yet all the same, she remained. %NThis was, in part, because she had nowhere else to go.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000652)
During his coma, she had been his lone caretaker. The couch in the%Nroom had become her bed, and even now, after he had awoken, she%Nstill used it as such.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000692)
【梨深２】
“I brought you something to eat.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006A2)
She spoke with warmth and sincerity as she held out a bag of food%Nshe had brought from the convenience store.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006B2)
Her words scared away the static atmosphere, and breathed new life%Ninto the dead world that surrounded them.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000006C2)
The girl surrendered herself to such an illusion, but did not%Nmention this to the boy as she laid several kinds of bread atop%Nthe empty bed.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000702)
【梨深２】
“Hey, this’s been on my mind for a while now, but... is food like%Nthis enough to keep you healthy?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000712)
【将軍？】
“I don’t have much time left as it is. Regardless, I’m sorry for%Nsending you out to buy these.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000752)
【梨深２】
“...It’s all right. Really. I got some food for myself, too, so%Ndon’t worry about it.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000076A)
She forced herself to smile at the boy. Then, taking an egg%Nsandwich for herself, she moved toward the window.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000786)
Upon opening the window, the crisp autumn breeze permeated the%Nquiet hospital room. Comfortably greeted by the wind, the girl%Nnarrowed her eyes and perched nimbly on the windowsill.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000796)
The room was located considerably high up. Imaginably, falling%Nwould mean certain death.
<LINE>
This, however, hardly mattered to the girl, who simply took a%Nhearty bite out of her sandwich.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000007A6)
The boy in the wheelchair paid her no heed.
<LINE>
He did not even attempt to reach for the bread laid out on the bed.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000806)
【梨深２】
“Listen, I need to ask you again... Are you really going to try to%Nawaken ‘him’?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000816)
【将軍？】
“I am. The chat the two of us had yesterday made that very clear%Nto me. NOZOMI has been keeping an eye on ‘him,’ and Noah II is%Nnearing completion. We must make haste.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000826)
【梨深２】
“No matter what it takes?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000836)
【将軍？】
“...That’s right.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000846)
【梨深２】
“But... that makes us no better than NOZOMI.%NScaring ‘him’... pushing him to the edge...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000856)
【将軍？】
“‘He’ is all we have.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000866)
【梨深２】
“...But if ‘he’ awakens, you’ll die.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000876)
【将軍？】
“I’ve been prepared for that from the very beginning. My death is%Nsuitable punishment for shoving all my responsibilities onto%N‘him.’”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000886)
The girl kept her gaze focused on the setting sun, not daring to%Nlook over her shoulder at the boy.
<LINE>
Her countenance laid her emotions bare; she looked as if she might%Nburst into tears at any moment.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000896)
【梨深２】
“Could... erasing ‘him’ be an option...?”%K%N

“If that were to happen, I would not hesitate to put myself through another year-long coma so that I could create another ‘me.’”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008A6)
【将軍？】
“Perhaps even longer. But by the time I would succeed, Noah II%Nwill have long since been completed—an event that shall cast the%Nworld into despair.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008B6)
Despite his gentle tone, his words were laced with a touch of%Ncynicism. Upon hearing them, the girl couldn’t help but let out a%Nsigh.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008C6)
【梨深２】
“I can’t support the way you’re going about this.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008D6)
【将軍？】
“We cannot allow Noah II to reach completion.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008E6)
【梨深２】
“I know we can’t, but... putting myself in ‘his’ shoes... it’s just so sad...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000008F6)
【梨深２】
“And there’s no way I can just stand around and watch while you%Nkill yourself.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000906)
【将軍？】
“I’m doing nothing of the sort.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000916)
【梨深２】
“...I’ll take care of it.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000926)
The boy finally moved a little, taken aback by the girl’s abrupt,%Nyet resolute words.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000936)
【将軍？】
“What exactly do you mean by that?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000962)
Finishing off the last of her sandwich, she stepped down from the%Nwindowsill, then turned to face him. Then, for some inexplicable%Nreason, she snapped into a pose resembling that of a salute.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009A2)
【梨深２】
“I swear to protect ‘him’ from NOZOMI.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009B2)
【梨深２】
“That way, you won’t have to die.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000009C2)
【将軍？】
“But that negates the very reason ‘he’ was created, and it doesn’t%Nsolve anything. Noah II—”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000A02)
【梨深２】
“I’ll take care of Noah II as well.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000A12)
【将軍？】
“...That just isn’t something you can handle.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000A22)
【梨深２】
“I’ve already made up my mind.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000A62)
【梨深２】
“I won’t let you do what you plan to do. I’m going to protect you.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000A72)
She gave him a frail, yet tender smile.
<LINE>
At the sight of this, the boy lost any and all words he had.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000AB2)
【梨深２】
“You predicted there’ll be another incident today, right?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000AC2)
【将軍？】
“It isn’t just a prediction—it’s an absolute fact. I have ‘seen’%Ntheir delusion myself.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000AD2)
【梨深２】
“If that’s true, then I can’t let ‘him’ get involved.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000AE2)
【梨深２】
“I’ll be going now.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000AFA)
She approached the door.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B0A)
【将軍？】
“Even if you interfere, I will still force ‘him’ to awaken as%Nplanned.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B26)
As she opened the door, hearing the boy’s words directed at her%Nback, she paused for one final time.%NNo signs of life came from the hallway. Not a single human being%Nwas in sight, and not a single sound reached the room.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B36)
【梨深２】
“Hey... just what are we, exactly? The two of us’ve been here for%Nover a year, all while nobody even knows we exist.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B46)
【梨深２】
“Being here, I can’t help but feel like my existence is nothing%Nmore than an illusion or something.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B56)
【梨深２】
“...Tahaha, I think this hospital’s gloominess is getting to my%Nhead.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B66)
【将軍？】
“Rimi... You shouldn’t get involved.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B76)
Despite the boy’s pleading...
<LINE>
the girl did not look back.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000B86)
【梨深２】
“Make sure to eat the bread I got you, okay?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00000BA2)
After murmuring those last few words, the girl left the hospital%Nroom.
<END>
